  "causal_findings": [
    "LSCore emits only a TextPart from agent response text. Valid ATI JSON survives as text; no schema validation or ATI DataPart/domain outcome mapping occurs.",
    "Consequently, an ATI record with status=failed is still LSCore A2A completed and MAS success=true when the model execution itself finishes normally.",
    "MAS source inspection shows typed-part extraction in the converter, but the provider/node result path returns text and metadata without preserving a typed domain result. Native LSCore requests here returned text only.",
    "After an actual successful A tool read, failed B tool read, and model HTTP500, LSCore correctly reports failed but returns no final artifact containing the successful evidence. The evidence exists only in the raw tool log in this experiment."
  ],
  "proposed_fixes": [
    "Construct and validate the ATI outcome deterministically from the execution/tool record at an application adapter boundary; emit a versioned DataPart plus human-readable text and map failed outcomes to A2A failed.",
    "Preserve conversion.data and artifact references through the MAS provider and node; carry domain outcome separately from transport completion so partial remains explicit.",
    "On fatal model/runtime errors, finalize a partial/failed record from already collected successful tool evidence before returning the terminal A2A event."
  ],
